Package: bsfa
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Stochastic Frontier Analysis
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person(given = "Franz X.",
                  family = "Mohr",
                  email = "franz.x.mohr@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Markov chain Monte Carlo methods for the Bayesian estimation of
    stochastic frontier models. Gibbs samplers with data augmentation are
    provided for composed-error frontier models in the tradition of
    van den Broeck, Koop, Osiewalski and Steel (1994), covering exponential
    and half-normal inefficiency, production and cost frontiers, and
    cross-sectional as well as time-invariant panel specifications. A model is
    built up step by step, by creating a model object and then adding priors,
    initial values and a seed to it before the posterior is drawn. Posterior
    distributions of unit-specific efficiency scores are obtained directly
    from the augmented draws rather than from point predictors.
